---
import {
  dielectricModelDefaults,
  polarModeResponse,
} from '../../../data/part07/dielectricOpticsModel.mjs';

const width = 650;
const height = 300;
const left = 58;
const right = 620;
const top = 34;
const bottom = 250;
const maxOmega = 1.6;
const xMap = (omega) => left + (right - left) * omega / maxOmega;
const yMap = (value) => bottom - Math.min(value, 6) * (bottom - top) / 6;
const curveFor = (strength) => Array.from({ length: 361 }, (_, index) => {
  const omega = maxOmega * index / 360;
  return {
    omega,
    loss: polarModeResponse({
      omega,
      epsilonInfinity: dielectricModelDefaults.epsilonInfinity,
      strength,
      omegaTO: dielectricModelDefaults.omegaTO,
      damping: dielectricModelDefaults.damping,
    }).lossFunction,
  };
});
const pathFor = (samples) => samples
  .map((point, index) => `${index === 0 ? 'M' : 'L'} ${xMap(point.omega).toFixed(2)} ${yMap(point.loss).toFixed(2)}`)
  .join(' ');
const defaults = polarModeResponse({
  omega: 1,
  epsilonInfinity: dielectricModelDefaults.epsilonInfinity,
  strength: dielectricModelDefaults.polarModeStrength,
  omegaTO: dielectricModelDefaults.omegaTO,
  damping: dielectricModelDefaults.damping,
});
const defaultPath = pathFor(curveFor(dielectricModelDefaults.polarModeStrength));
const fallbackCases = [0.6, 1.8, 3.0].map((strength) => ({
  strength,
  ...polarModeResponse({
    omega: 1,
    epsilonInfinity: dielectricModelDefaults.epsilonInfinity,
    strength,
    omegaTO: dielectricModelDefaults.omegaTO,
    damping: dielectricModelDefaults.damping,
  }),
}));
---

<figure class="chapter-visual polar-mode" data-polar-mode>
  <figcaption>
    <strong>原创交互模型：单极性模的晶格介电响应与 LO–TO splitting</strong>
    <span lang="en">Original interactive model: lattice dielectric response and LO–TO splitting of one polar mode</span>
  </figcaption>

  <div class="chapter-visual__controls polar-mode__controls">
    <label>
      <span>mode oscillator strength S | 模式强度</span>
      <input type="range" min="0.4" max="3" step="0.1" value={dielectricModelDefaults.polarModeStrength} data-polar-strength />
      <output data-polar-strength-output>{dielectricModelDefaults.polarModeStrength.toFixed(1)}</output>
    </label>
    <label>
      <span>probe frequency ω | 探测频率</span>
      <input type="range" min="0" max={maxOmega} step="0.02" value="1.00" data-polar-omega />
      <output data-polar-omega-output>1.00</output>
    </label>
  </div>

  <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${width} ${height}`} role="img" aria-labelledby="polar-title polar-desc">
    <title id="polar-title">Loss function of a single polar lattice mode</title>
    <desc id="polar-desc">
      The transverse optical frequency is fixed at 0.75. A keyboard-operable oscillator-strength control changes the static dielectric constant and shifts the zero of the dielectric function, marked as the longitudinal optical frequency. The loss function peaks near the longitudinal frequency.
    </desc>
    <line x1={left} y1={bottom} x2={right} y2={bottom} class="plot-axis" />
    <line x1={left} y1={top} x2={left} y2={bottom} class="plot-axis" />
    <line x1={xMap(dielectricModelDefaults.omegaTO)} y1={top} x2={xMap(dielectricModelDefaults.omegaTO)} y2={bottom} class="polar-mode__to" />
    <line x1={xMap(defaults.omegaLO)} y1={top} x2={xMap(defaults.omegaLO)} y2={bottom} class="polar-mode__lo" data-polar-lo-line />
    <path d={defaultPath} class="plot-curve" data-polar-path />
    <line x1={xMap(1)} y1={top} x2={xMap(1)} y2={bottom} class="polar-mode__probe" data-polar-probe />
    <text x={right} y="280" text-anchor="end">ω</text>
    <text x="16" y="48">−Im ε⁻¹</text>
    <text x={xMap(dielectricModelDefaults.omegaTO) - 8} y="52" text-anchor="end">TO</text>
    <text x={xMap(defaults.omegaLO) + 8} y="72" data-polar-lo-label>LO</text>
  </svg>

  <div class="chapter-visual__readout polar-mode__readout" aria-live="polite">
    <span>ωTO</span><strong>{dielectricModelDefaults.omegaTO.toFixed(3)}</strong>
    <span>ωLO</span><strong data-polar-lo>{defaults.omegaLO.toFixed(3)}</strong>
    <span>ε(0)</span><strong data-polar-static>{defaults.epsilonStatic.toFixed(3)}</strong>
    <span>ε(0)/ε∞</span><strong data-polar-lst>{defaults.lstRatio.toFixed(4)}</strong>
    <span>(ωLO/ωTO)²</span><strong data-polar-frequency-ratio>{defaults.frequencyRatioSquared.toFixed(4)}</strong>
    <span>loss at probe</span><strong data-polar-loss>{defaults.lossFunction.toFixed(4)}</strong>
  </div>

  <div class="polar-mode__fallback">
    <p><strong>无 JavaScript 参考表 | No-JavaScript reference table</strong></p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>S</th><th>ωLO</th><th>ε(0)</th><th>LST ratio</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {fallbackCases.map((entry) => (
          <tr>
            <td>{entry.strength.toFixed(1)}</td>
            <td>{entry.omegaLO.toFixed(3)}</td>
            <td>{entry.epsilonStatic.toFixed(3)}</td>
            <td>{entry.lstRatio.toFixed(4)}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="chapter-visual__contract">
    <p><strong>模型：</strong><code>ε(ω)=ε∞+S/(ωTO²−ω²−iγω)</code>，固定 <code>ε∞=2.5</code>、<code>ωTO=0.75</code>、<code>γ=0.08</code>；<code>ωLO²=ωTO²+S/ε∞</code>。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Model:</strong> <code>ε(ω)=ε∞+S/(ωTO²−ω²−iγω)</code> with fixed <code>ε∞=2.5</code>, <code>ωTO=0.75</code>, and <code>γ=0.08</code>; <code>ωLO²=ωTO²+S/ε∞</code>.</p>
    <p><strong>验收：</strong><code>S→0</code> 时 LO–TO splitting 消失；对任意正 S，<code>ε(0)/ε∞=(ωLO/ωTO)²</code>；loss peak 位于 LO 附近而 Im ε 的 transverse resonance 位于 TO 附近。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Acceptance:</strong> as <code>S→0</code>, LO–TO splitting vanishes; for positive S, <code>ε(0)/ε∞=(ωLO/ωTO)²</code>; the loss peak lies near LO while the transverse Im ε resonance lies near TO.</p>
    <p><strong>边界：</strong>这是无量纲、单模式、各向同性、固定 E 边界的教学模型。真实晶体需要 Born tensors、mode eigenvectors、masses、direction-dependent ε∞ 和 nonanalytic dynamical matrix。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Boundary:</strong> this is a dimensionless, single-mode, isotropic teaching model at fixed E. A real crystal requires Born tensors, mode eigenvectors, masses, direction-dependent ε∞, and the nonanalytic dynamical matrix.</p>
  </div>
</figure>

<script>
  import {
    dielectricModelDefaults,
    polarModeResponse,
  } from '../../../data/part07/dielectricOpticsModel.mjs';

  document.querySelectorAll('[data-polar-mode]').forEach((root) => {
    const strengthInput = root.querySelector('[data-polar-strength]');
    const omegaInput = root.querySelector('[data-polar-omega]');
    const strengthOutput = root.querySelector('[data-polar-strength-output]');
    const omegaOutput = root.querySelector('[data-polar-omega-output]');
    const loOutput = root.querySelector('[data-polar-lo]');
    const staticOutput = root.querySelector('[data-polar-static]');
    const lstOutput = root.querySelector('[data-polar-lst]');
    const ratioOutput = root.querySelector('[data-polar-frequency-ratio]');
    const lossOutput = root.querySelector('[data-polar-loss]');
    const path = root.querySelector('[data-polar-path]');
    const loLine = root.querySelector('[data-polar-lo-line]');
    const loLabel = root.querySelector('[data-polar-lo-label]');
    const probe = root.querySelector('[data-polar-probe]');
    if (!(strengthInput instanceof HTMLInputElement) || !(omegaInput instanceof HTMLInputElement)) return;

    const left = 58;
    const right = 620;
    const top = 34;
    const bottom = 250;
    const maxOmega = 1.6;
    const xMap = (omega) => left + (right - left) * omega / maxOmega;
    const yMap = (value) => bottom - Math.min(value, 6) * (bottom - top) / 6;

    const update = () => {
      const strength = Number(strengthInput.value);
      const omega = Number(omegaInput.value);
      const response = polarModeResponse({
        omega,
        epsilonInfinity: dielectricModelDefaults.epsilonInfinity,
        strength,
        omegaTO: dielectricModelDefaults.omegaTO,
        damping: dielectricModelDefaults.damping,
      });
      const curve = Array.from({ length: 361 }, (_, index) => {
        const sampleOmega = maxOmega * index / 360;
        return {
          omega: sampleOmega,
          loss: polarModeResponse({
            omega: sampleOmega,
            epsilonInfinity: dielectricModelDefaults.epsilonInfinity,
            strength,
            omegaTO: dielectricModelDefaults.omegaTO,
            damping: dielectricModelDefaults.damping,
          }).lossFunction,
        };
      }).map((point, index) => `${index === 0 ? 'M' : 'L'} ${xMap(point.omega).toFixed(2)} ${yMap(point.loss).toFixed(2)}`).join(' ');
      if (path instanceof SVGPathElement) path.setAttribute('d', curve);
      if (loLine instanceof SVGLineElement) {
        loLine.setAttribute('x1', xMap(response.omegaLO).toFixed(2));
        loLine.setAttribute('x2', xMap(response.omegaLO).toFixed(2));
      }
      if (loLabel instanceof SVGTextElement) loLabel.setAttribute('x', (xMap(response.omegaLO) + 8).toFixed(2));
      if (probe instanceof SVGLineElement) {
        probe.setAttribute('x1', xMap(omega).toFixed(2));
        probe.setAttribute('x2', xMap(omega).toFixed(2));
      }
      if (strengthOutput instanceof HTMLOutputElement) strengthOutput.value = strength.toFixed(1);
      if (omegaOutput instanceof HTMLOutputElement) omegaOutput.value = omega.toFixed(2);
      if (loOutput instanceof HTMLElement) loOutput.textContent = response.omegaLO.toFixed(3);
      if (staticOutput instanceof HTMLElement) staticOutput.textContent = response.epsilonStatic.toFixed(3);
      if (lstOutput instanceof HTMLElement) lstOutput.textContent = response.lstRatio.toFixed(4);
      if (ratioOutput instanceof HTMLElement) ratioOutput.textContent = response.frequencyRatioSquared.toFixed(4);
      if (lossOutput instanceof HTMLElement) lossOutput.textContent = response.lossFunction.toFixed(4);
    };
    strengthInput.addEventListener('input', update);
    omegaInput.addEventListener('input', update);
    update();
  });
</script>

<style>
  .polar-mode { overflow-x: auto; }
  .polar-mode svg { width: 100%; min-width: 38rem; }
  .polar-mode text { fill: currentColor; font-size: 13px; }
  .polar-mode__to { stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-2); stroke-width: 1.6; stroke-dasharray: 5 4; }
  .polar-mode__lo { stroke: var(--sl-color-accent-high); stroke-width: 1.8; }
  .polar-mode__probe { stroke: currentColor; stroke-width: 1; stroke-dasharray: 2 3; }
  .polar-mode__controls { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; }
  .polar-mode__controls label { display: grid; gap: 0.35rem; }
  .polar-mode__readout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(8rem, 1fr)); gap: 0.4rem 1rem; }
  .polar-mode__fallback { max-width: 38rem; }
</style>
